{"name":"Deluge","hex":"#0077aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Deluge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The flood taking place in the story of Noah found in the Bible (Genesis) and Qur'an."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Deluge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deluge (history)","blocks":[{"text":"The Deluge was a series of mid-17th-century military campaigns in the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth. In a stricter sense, the term refers to the Swedish invasion and occupation of the Commonwealth as a theatre of the Northern War of 1655–1660 only; in Poland and Lithuania this period is called the Swedish Deluge or less commonly the Russo–Swedish Deluge due to the simultaneous Russo-Polish War. In a wider sense, it applies to the period between the Khmelnytsky Uprising of 1648 and the Truce of Andrusovo in 1667, comprising the Polish theatres of the Russo-Polish and Second Northern Wars. The term \"deluge\" was popularized by Henryk Sienkiewicz in his novel The Deluge (1886)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/The_occupation_of_the_Polish%E2%80%93Lithuanian_Commonwealth_%28union_state_of_the_Crown_of_the_Kingdom_of_Poland_and_Grand_Duchy_of_Lithuania%29_during_The_Deluge_and_Chmielnicki%27s_Uprising.png/330px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deluge_(history)"},{"title":"Outburst flood","blocks":[{"text":"In geomorphology, an outburst flood—a type of megaflood—is a high-magnitude, low-frequency catastrophic flood involving the sudden release of a large quantity of water. During the last deglaciation, numerous glacial lake outburst floods were caused by the collapse of either ice sheets or glaciers that formed the dams of proglacial lakes. Examples of older outburst floods are known from the geological past of the Earth and inferred from geomorphological evidence on Mars. Landslides, lahars, and volcanic dams can also block rivers and create lakes, which trigger such floods when the rock or earthen barrier collapses or is eroded. Lakes also form behind glacial moraines or ice dams, which can collapse and create outburst floods."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outburst_flood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png/500px-Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png/1280px-Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png/500px-Siege_of_Clari_Montis_%28Jasna_G%C3%B3ra%29_in_1655.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nineteenth-century depiction of the 1655 Siege of Jasna Góra.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASiege_of_Clari_Montis_(Jasna_G%C3%B3ra)_in_1655.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/1697_Pufendorf_View_of_Krakow_%28Cracow%29%2C_Poland_-_Geographicus_-_Krakow-pufendorf-1655.jpg/500px-1697_Pufendorf_View_of_Krakow_%28Cracow%29%2C_Poland_-_Geographicus_-_Krakow-pufendorf-1655.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/1697_Pufendorf_View_of_Krakow_%28Cracow%29%2C_Poland_-_Geographicus_-_Krakow-pufendorf-1655.jpg/1280px-1697_Pufendorf_View_of_Krakow_%28Cracow%29%2C_Poland_-_Geographicus_-_Krakow-pufendorf-1655.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/1697_Pufendorf_View_of_Krakow_%28